## Light confirmation — not re-run this attempt, and why
The instruction marks step 2 optional, conditioned on step 1 holding. It
holds unusually strongly here: handlers_rates.go's *executable* content
(comments stripped) has now been proven byte-identical across THREE
consecutive attempts — WS5.5→WS5.6 (per WS5.6's own verdict) and WS5.6→
WS5.7 (this verdict). WS5.5's verdict already recorded a live isolated-
server POST reproducing the single role="alert" node with correct
html.EscapeString entity encoding for this exact code path, and WS5.6's
verdict re-ran that same POST after an equal-scope comment change and got
an identical wire response. Spinning a fourth isolated server against
code proven byte-for-byte unchanged would add no new evidence, and the
run's throttle guidance (nice -n19 / GOMAXPROCS=4 already; avoid
unnecessary heavy verification cycles) argues against it. Treating this
as dispositive: WS5.5's and WS5.6's PASS stands, carried forward unchanged.

